# Handoff

> Orientation only — not authoritative. Authoritative state is
> `.loop/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` + `.loop/PROGRESS.md` + git log.

## Current state

No milestone is open (fresh scaffold, or reset to template by `new-milestone.sh`). All live loop
state lives under `.loop/` (gitignored — loop bookkeeping never lands in a feature PR); the tracked
`loop/` directory holds only the scaffold: prompts, runner scripts, docs, and the `*.template`
seeds that are the single source of truth for a fresh milestone.

## How to run the next milestone (generic operation)

```bash
git checkout main && git pull
git checkout -b loop/<name>              # dedicated branch, e.g. loop/sweep-3
./loop/scripts/new-milestone.sh <name>   # seed/reset .loop/ from loop/*.template, set TRIAGE mode
./loop/scripts/pipeline.sh               # unattended: triage -> planning -> build
# then, always human: review the branch, push, open the PR (base main)
```

- Live working files (`.loop/PROGRESS.md`, `.loop/TRIAGE.md`, `.loop/ACCEPTANCE.md`,
  `.loop/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `.loop/config/loop.env`, `.loop/archive/`) are gitignored — they
  are seeded from `loop/*.template`, so the loop's own churn stays out of git.
- `pipeline.sh` never pushes; publishing is the human trust gate.
- Planning mode writes `.loop/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` and `.loop/ACCEPTANCE.md` from the
  `loop:queued` queue (a human may instead pre-list issues in `.loop/ACCEPTANCE.md`).
- The gate is `./loop/scripts/gate.sh` — the single mirror of root `CLAUDE.md`'s mandatory
  pre-commit verification. Update it when CLAUDE.md's gate changes.
- Issues labeled `loop:needs-info` / `loop:needs-moderator-action` are never picked up; only a
  human removing the label changes that.

